{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>For you shall surely perish.</b> This is a doubling of expression, and so too the doubling of destruction that he mentioned, and so too the doubling of the making that he mentioned, for he said 'and you shall make a carved image,' 'and you will do what is evil,' etc. It is possible to explain according to the way of the midrash that our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Lamentations Rabbah 1:57): they sinned doubly, as it is said (Lamentations 1:8): 'Jerusalem has grievously sinned [lit. sinned a sin]'; and they were punished doubly, as it is said (Isaiah 40:2): 'for she has received double for all her sins'; and they are comforted doubly, as it is said (Isaiah 40:1): 'Comfort, comfort my people.' But would it enter your mind that they were punished doubly more than they sinned? For this is not the way of the Master of mercy, blessed be He, and likewise one must understand what the doubling of the sin is." "Rather, this is its explanation: for it is said (Jeremiah 2:13), 'For my people have committed two evils: they have forsaken me, the fountain of living waters, and hewn out for themselves cisterns, broken cisterns' — behold, one evil that is two. For had they served Him in partnership, at the very least it would have been one evil, namely the joining of the name of Heaven with something else. But 'they have forsaken me' entirely — even in partnership they did not serve Him, and this is one doubled evil, namely idolatry and the abandonment of HaShem, blessed be He. Therefore their punishment was doubled in this manner, for HaShem forsook Israel and filled the cities of the nations, as it is said (Ezekiel 26:2): 'I shall be filled with the destroyed city' — Tyre was not filled except from the destruction of Jerusalem. And had both been desolate, Jerusalem would have had the consolation of another's suffering; but now that this one rises and that one falls, behold she has received double for all her sins — it is not said 'for her sins' but 'for all her sins,' but rather He wished to say that along with her doubled sins she received also a doubled punishment of blows in this manner. And likewise the consolation will be doubled, in the abandonment of the nations and the success of Israel.\n\nTherefore it is said here: 'and you shall make a carved image' — behold the making of idolatry; 'and you will do what is evil in the eyes of HaShem your Elohim, to provoke Him' — behold a second making, that even in partnership they would not serve Him, for everyone who provokes does not serve. Therefore He doubled the perishing and the destruction, as it is said, 'for she has received double.' And concerning this He said: 'and you will be left few in number among the nations where HaShem will lead you' — behold that the lands of the nations will be full, while your land is a desolation. And after He said: 'and you will return to HaShem,' etc., He said: 'to dispossess nations greater and mightier than you from before you,' etc. — this is the doubled consolation that will be in the future, as it was on the day of their going up from the land of Egypt."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:11:29.968577102Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}